          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+theory"} graph theory
            a
            %em pseudograph
            is a particular type of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
            and for each unordered pair of vertices a set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
            between these.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed
            pseudograph is also called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
          %p The terminology is used in distinction to:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multigraphs"} multigraphs
                , which are like pseudographs but not admitted to have “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loops"}> loops
                ” in the sense of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
                between a vertex and itself;
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+graphs"} simple graphs
                , which are multigraphs with at most one edge between any unordered pair of distinct vertices.
          %p
            Beware that the terminology is not completely consistent across different authors. Some authors may allows
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loops"} loops
            when they speak of multigraphs.
          %p
            From yet another perspective, pseudographs are also like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+categories"} dagger categories
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            forgotten. Conversely, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+category"} dagger category
            may be regarded as a pseudograph equipped with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi DagCat
                  %mo →
                  %mi Pseudograph
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon DagCat \to Pseudograph
          %p
            where Pseudograph is the category of pseudographs and
            %span.newWikiWord
              DagCat
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/DagCat"} ?
            is the category of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Pseudograph
                  %mo →
                  %mi DagCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon Pseudograph \to DagCat
          %p
            sending each pseudograph to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free dagger category
            on that pseudograph.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#slick_definition Slick definition
          %p
            A
            %strong pseudograph
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with a contravariant quiver homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo †
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\dagger:G \to G^\op
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to the opposite quiver
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^\op
            which
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                is the identity on
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            %li
              %p
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo †
                        %mo ∘
                        %mo †
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                          %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger \circ \dagger = \mathrm{id}_G
          %h3#nuts_and_bolts_definition Nuts and bolts definition
          %p
            A
            %strong pseudograph
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E, V, s, t)
            with a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
